From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:08:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ucode: update to OpenWrt main's ucode (2026-10-28, dfc64d41)

Take OpenWrt main's ucode package as of 3e6064bb (ucode dfc64d41, ABI
20261009, up from b885dd0f of 2026-07-09 and ABI 20230711). It brings
the uloop fixes that cannot be backported on their own: fired one-shot
timers are released (115d308a, B70, ~130 bytes leaked per timer) and a
finished uloop.task() closes its pipes (the task rework, 1f54bd28, B72,
one descriptor leaked per task), along with everything in the 306
commits between, of which the port carried the ubus prototype fix
(B116), require(), map() under GC and SO_TIMESTAMPNS as backports.

Drop those backports (010-015) and OpenWrt's old 100, 110 and 111,
which are all in dfc64d41. Keep the port's 120 and 121 (reconnect to
ubusd), which apply unchanged.

The ABI version changes, so libucode20230711 becomes libucode20261009
and every ucode module and user is rebuilt.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
