-From 153c627fd44566b65e9694f9155842f5475315ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
-Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:59:12 +0200
-Subject: [PATCH] lib: do not store a failed module in the module table
-
-uc_require_path() stores the result of a load in the module table as
-soon as the file exists, also if the module raised an exception. The
-next import() or require() of that name then returns the incomplete
-result of the failed load, for example an empty namespace, and raises
-no error.
-
-Store the module only if the load raised no exception, so that a later
-load runs the module again.
-
-Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
